export default "<section class=\"block \" id=\"flows\">\n      <h2>How data flows</h2>\n      <p>Which tables change, in order, for the three things you do most.</p>\n      <div class=\"flows\"><div class=\"flow\" id=\"flow-sale\"><h3>When a cashier sells</h3><ol><li><a class=\"tref\" href=\"#t-shifts\"><code>shifts</code></a><span>The cashier opens a shift with the cash in the drawer.</span></li><li><a class=\"tref\" href=\"#t-sales\"><code>sales</code></a><span>Paying creates one sales row with a receipt number (store code + number from stores.receipt_seq).</span></li><li><a class=\"tref\" href=\"#t-sale-items\"><code>sale_items</code></a><span>One row per line, with the name, price, options and promotion copied from the menu.</span></li><li><a class=\"tref\" href=\"#t-payments\"><code>payments</code></a><span>One row per way of paying (cash, KHQR, card, wallet...).</span></li><li><a class=\"tref\" href=\"#t-inventory\"><code>inventory</code></a><span>Stock goes down for items with track_stock on (or their recipe ingredients), and a stock_movements row records it.</span></li><li><a class=\"tref\" href=\"#t-loyalty-transactions\"><code>loyalty_transactions</code></a><span>If a member was added, points earned or redeemed are recorded and customers.points changes.</span></li><li><a class=\"tref\" href=\"#t-z-reports\"><code>z_reports</code></a><span>At the end of the day, the Z report saves the day&#x27;s totals for the store.</span></li></ol></div><div class=\"flow\" id=\"flow-sync\"><h3>When the admin syncs the BROWN menu</h3><ol><li><a class=\"tref\" href=\"#t-stores\"><code>stores</code></a><span>The POS reads the store&#x27;s external_id (its BROWN id) and calls the BROWN API.</span></li><li><a class=\"tref\" href=\"#t-categories\"><code>categories</code></a><span>Each BROWN group (Beverages...) becomes a top-level category, and its categories go under it (Beverages &gt; Hot Drinks).</span></li><li><a class=\"tref\" href=\"#t-products\"><code>products</code></a><span>Each item is matched by SKU (BROWN item_id): new ones are created, existing ones get the new name, picture and category.</span></li><li><a class=\"tref\" href=\"#t-inventory\"><code>inventory</code></a><span>Each item is listed in the store (is_listed). If the store&#x27;s BROWN price differs from the base price, it goes into price_override.</span></li><li><a class=\"tref\" href=\"#t-product-options\"><code>product_options</code></a><span>Each drink gets its sizes (from detail.prices: fcode 1 = S, 2 = M, 3 = L) with this store&#x27;s prices, and its own options and add-ons.</span></li><li><a class=\"tref\" href=\"#t-audit-logs\"><code>audit_logs</code></a><span>A BROWN_MENU_SYNCED row records who synced which store and the counts (never the token).</span></li></ol></div><div class=\"flow\" id=\"flow-price\"><h3>How the POS finds an item&#x27;s price</h3><ol><li><a class=\"tref\" href=\"#t-inventory\"><code>inventory</code></a><span>Take the row for this product and this store. If is_listed is off, the store does not sell it.</span></li><li><a class=\"tref\" href=\"#t-inventory\"><code>inventory</code></a><span>If price_override has a value, that is the price in this store.</span></li><li><a class=\"tref\" href=\"#t-products\"><code>products</code></a><span>Otherwise the price is products.sell_price.</span></li><li><a class=\"tref\" href=\"#t-product-options\"><code>product_options</code></a><span>If the drink has its own options in this store (sizes from BROWN), add their price_delta (M +0.50, L +1.10...).</span></li><li><a class=\"tref\" href=\"#t-modifier-options\"><code>modifier_options</code></a><span>Otherwise add the option&#x27;s normal price_delta (Oat milk +0.60...).</span></li><li><a class=\"tref\" href=\"#t-promotions\"><code>promotions</code></a><span>Take off the biggest promotion that fits the item, the store, the day and the time.</span></li><li><a class=\"tref\" href=\"#t-stores\"><code>stores</code></a><span>Add tax with stores.tax_rate if the product is taxable.</span></li></ol></div></div>\n    </section>";
